FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.441, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0023", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4364, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4211, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4203, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0092", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4146, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0089", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.0518, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 60, "dropped_candidates": 334, "token_estimate": 31959, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Both companies describe heavy dependence on advertising and risks from reduced advertiser spending and changes to ad targeting. Google says it generated more than 70% of total revenues from online advertising in 2025, and that advertisers and partners can terminate contracts at any time [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]. Meta says it generates substantially all of its revenue from advertising and that marketers have no long-term advertising commitments [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0008]. Google highlights ad-blocking and personalization-limiting technologies, new ad formats shaped by AI, and macroeconomic sensitivity [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. Meta highlights reduced targeting and measurement from user data practice changes and mobile platform changes such as Apple's iOS changes [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015]. The filings do not rank these risks, so no ordering of severity is given.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "GOOG", "company": "Alphabet Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Alphabet generated more than 70% of total revenues from online advertising in 2025 (FY2025, ended December 31, 2025), and advertisers, distributors, publishers and content providers can terminate contracts at any time.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Alphabet cites AI reshaping advertising, with no assurance that it will adapt effectively, and technologies that make personalized ads more difficult or block ads altogether.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Alphabet says advertiser expenditures tend to correlate with overall economic conditions, and its revenue growth rate could decline from factors including deceleration or declines in advertiser spending.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001", "GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "META", "company": "Meta Platforms Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Meta says substantially all revenue comes from marketers advertising on Facebook and Instagram, without long-term commitments, and loss of marketers or reduced spending could seriously harm its business.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0008"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta says changes to its user data practices and regulatory frameworks have limited its ability to target and measure ads and negatively impacted advertising revenue, including marketer reaction to iOS changes beginning in 2021.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta lists further factors that can affect advertising revenue, including decreases in user engagement, third-party policy changes by Apple and Google, and user shifts toward products such as Reels that monetize at a lower rate.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009", "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0023"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Theme", "Alphabet (GOOG)", "Meta (META)"], "rows": [["Advertising dependence", "More than 70% of total revenues from online advertising in 2025 [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]", "Substantially all revenue from advertising [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0008]"], ["Advertiser commitments", "Many advertisers and partners can terminate contracts at any time [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]", "Marketers do not have long-term advertising commitments [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0008]"], ["Targeting and personalization", "Technologies make personalized ads more difficult or block ads [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]", "Data practice changes reduce ad targeting ability [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015]